& .\tools\peer.ps1 -Agent codex -Slug vi-error-list-by-script -TimeoutSec 240 -Task "Factual API question, search NI docs/forums/LabVIEW Wiki, cite URLs. LabVIEW 2026 64-bit, VI Scripting enabled, driving LabVIEW from Python over ActiveX/COM (VI Server). A VI assembled by VI Scripting is BROKEN (VI.ExecState = 0 / eBad). Question 1: is there any VI Server property or method (public, scripting-scope, or private/SuperSecretPrivateSpecialStuff) that returns the VI's Error List text programmatically - i.e. the same items the Error list window (Ctrl+L) shows, such as 'Wire: type conflict' or 'SubVI is missing' - e.g. 'VI.Get Error List', 'ErrorList', 'VI.Errors', 'VI:Get VI Errors', 'Get Bad Wires', anything on the VI class or Application class? Give the exact name / ID and its scope. Question 2: failing that, which scripting-scope properties reveal WHY a VI is broken indirectly: e.g. Wire.IsBad / 'Bad Wires[]', Terminal type-conflict flags, SubVI 'VI Refnum'/'Is Missing', Node.Bad? Question 3: is there an Invoke method to open the Error List window from VI Server (so a screenshot can be taken without keyboard input)? Already known: VI.ExecState (0=bad) works; 'Remove Bad Wires' (method ID 410) works; the public VI class docs list no error-list accessor."
